-- title:
--   Regularity of the varpi-fibre along the Gauss branch, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ and subgroup `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$; that is, $K$ is generated over $L$ by the image of that function field under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ on Laurent series. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $A$ acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$, let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$, and let $j \in K$ be a nonzero element whose underlying Laurent series is the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, transported to $L$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ characterised by: $f \in W_0$ iff there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with the reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ after mapping coefficients to $L$ (the Gauss valuation ring of $A$-integral $q$-expansions). Consider the two-chart integral model [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ glued along their common localisation, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$. Let $z$ be a point of this model and let $\varpi_z$ be the germ at $z$ of the global section obtained from $\varpi$ via `toBase`, and assume $\varpi_z$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk at $z$. Assume further that $z$ is the image under the canonical morphism `ιFin` of a point $y$ of the finite chart, i.e. a prime ideal of the integral closure of $A[j]$ in $K$, that this prime is not maximal, and that every element of that integral closure which is a nonunit of $W_0$ lies in it. Then the quotient of the stalk at $z$ by the ideal generated by $\varpi_z$ is a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the assertion that the component of the special fibre of the integral model of $X(\Gamma_H(q^2M'))$ cut out by the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$ — the $\infty$-branch of the Igusa picture — is reduced at its generic point, equivalently that $W_0$ is unramified over $A$, in the case $q=3$. It feeds the construction of an open neighbourhood on which the structure morphism to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ is smooth, used in the analysis of semistable coverings of modular curves.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_not_isMaximal_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_twoChartIntegralModel_xH_of_eq_three.lean

